# FitConnect tooling governance

"Always use everything" means: **use every applicable, approved, compatible tool**. It does not mean install arbitrary MCP servers because they exist.

## Before significant work

1. Inspect installed Cursor plugins, project skills, `.cursor/rules`, `AGENTS.md`, `.mcp.json`, CI workflows, and platform SDKs.
2. Select tools that materially help this task.
3. Use all selected tools. Do not silently skip an applicable installed capability.
4. Record why a listed tool was not applicable when that distinction matters.

## Prefer

- Official, actively maintained open-source projects
- Permissive licenses
- Local / self-hosted / zero-recurring-cost tooling
- Least privilege (no production DB, secrets, or filesystem root on an MCP)

## Never

- Connect an unknown MCP to production credentials or databases
- Treat "free to install" as "free to operate"
- Print secrets, tokens, or env values
- Claim Web/Android/iOS verification from unit tests or `assembleDebug` alone
- Introduce Terra / Spike / ROOK as mandatory core dependencies
- Replace native Android/Compose or SwiftUI/iOS with Expo for UI
- Generate redundant tool calls just to satisfy a checklist

